No QtQuickTemplates2 headers in /opt/homebrew/include. So I need the framework version-dir approach. Let me update build.rs to discover and add the versioned Headers dir of QtQuickTemplates2.framework. Simpler: for each needed framework, add its `Headers/<version>` subdir if present.

Actually, the cleanest general solution: for framework modules, add `-I <framework>/Headers/<verdir>` for the versioned dir. Let me implement: for each framework dir `<libs>/<M>.framework/Headers`, find a single subdirectory (the version), add `-I <that>/<verdir>`.

Let me implement a helper in build.rs:

```rust
fn framework_header_dirs(libs: &str, framework: &str) -> Vec<String> {
    let base = PathBuf::from(libs).join(format!("{framework}.framework/Headers"));
    let mut dirs = vec![];
    if let Ok(rd) = std::fs::read_dir(&base) {
        for e in rd.flatten() {
            if e.file_type().map(|t| t.is_dir()).unwrap_or(false) {
                dirs.push(e.path().to_string_lossy().to_string());
            }
        }
    }
    dirs
}
```

