Actually, let me reconsider a simpler design that avoids the Templates2 include entirely — since the spike just needs to prove QML-signal→C++→Rust. 

Alternative clean approach that needs NO extra header: use `QMetaObject` connection via `QObject::connect` with the sender's *meta-signal index*... not exposed.

Or: QML side can call a function on an object we give it. But that object needs invokable methods → Q_OBJECT.

I think the QQuickAbstractButton route is the right one and it's exactly what the real renderer needs anyway (Button/TextField/Slider/Switch all expose real C++ signals via Templates2). Let me just make build.rs handle the framework header dirs.

