Let me design a shared function:
```rust
enum QtAction {
    Send(Event),
    Scheme(Scheme),
    None,
}

fn decode_event(raw: &QtEvent) -> QtAction {
    match raw.kind {
        ev::POINTER_DOWN => Send(Event::PointerDown { target, x, y, secondary: false }),
        ev::POINTER_MOVE => Send(Event::PointerMove { target, x, y, hovering: false, leaving: false }),
        ev::POINTER_UP => Send(Event::PointerUp { target, x, y, secondary: false }),
        ev::VALUE_CHANGED => Send(Event::ValueChanged { target, value }),
        ev::TEXT_CHANGED => Send(Event::TextChanged { target, value }),
        ev::NAVIGATE_BACK => Send(Event::Navigate { url: None }),
        ev::SCHEME_CHANGED => Scheme(if raw.value >= 0.5 { Dark } else { Light }),
        _ => None,
    }
}
```
Wait — Event::Navigate doesn't have a `target`. It's global. But the QtEvent struct has node_id; for NAVIGATE_BACK, node_id is 0 (ignored). OK.

Then in qt_event:
```rust
